Reading the BPFK definition of {e'i}
here<http://www.lojban.org/tiki/BPFK+Section%3A+Irrealis+Attitudinals>,
I feel like {.e'i do na broda} would translate to "You must not do
{broda}", while {e'i ko na broda} would translate to "Don't {broda}". If
this understanding is right, then there's no problem expressing what gleki
wants, and selpa'i is subtly wrong. If I'm wrong, could someone point me to
an explanation of why?


